  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273970/assets/65420a63daa7a7c4f7a4c061bfc4e7fd223d28cc90f7fbc7e02d4d6f066ec968.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3)=\\infty .\n$$",
